{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\nAllow fixing the Projects page to one board: `projects-board \"vig demo board\"` (title, case-insensitive) or `projects-board 2` (project number). When set, the page shows only that board (no `p` / `P` cycling); if the project is not linked to the repository, a notice names it. Top-level node like `theme` / `procs-refresh-interval` (replace-wholesale in a user config).\n\nBecomes really useful together with repository-local config (#132), where each repo can pin its own board.\n\n## Tasks\n- [ ] Loader accessor + validation (string or integer arg) + merge rule + tests\n- [ ] Projects state honours the pin (selection fixed, cycling disabled, not-linked notice)\n- [ ] docs/config.md + README mention\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T03:58:05Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":131,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Projects: pin the board with a `projects-board` config node"}
